WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.712
This example shows one of the most useful window
patterns placing group

00:00:03.738 --> 00:00:09.100
and overall averages beside each detail row AVG
salary OVER partition by

00:00:09.125 --> 00:00:14.150
department calculates a separate average for each
department Every employee in the

00:00:14.175 --> 00:00:19.850
same department receives the same department_average
value AVG salary OVER

00:00:19.875 --> 00:00:25.588
with empty parentheses calculates one average across
the entire result population Because

00:00:25.612 --> 00:00:30.200
there is no PARTITION BY every employee row receives
the same company_average

00:00:30.212 --> 00:00:35.650
value The employee row itself is not removed We
still see name

00:00:35.775 --> 00:00:40.700
department and salary That makes it easy to compare
one employee's salary

00:00:40.725 --> 00:00:45.000
with both local and global context Run the query and
choose one

00:00:45.025 --> 00:00:49.625
employee Compare that person's salary to the
department average and then to

00:00:49.638 --> 00:00:54.738
the company average This is a major difference from
GROUP BY A

00:00:54.750 --> 00:00:58.075
GROUP BY query could return one average row per
department but it

00:00:58.088 --> 00:01:03.075
would not automatically keep each employee row
beside that average Window functions

00:01:03.100 --> 00:01:06.538
are very powerful for feature engineering and
reporting because they let you

00:01:06.562 --> 00:01:09.388
add contextual measures without changing the detail
grain
